# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
# id: differential.ed2-preserves-cursor
# geometry: 80 24
# expect-cursor: 4 13
# expect-line: 0 =
#
# Erase-in-display (ED 2) clears every cell and leaves the cursor exactly
# where it was. The shell `clear` composite pairs ED 2 with a separate cursor
# home; conflating the two is a classic differential-testing false positive,
# so the cursor position is the assertion that matters here.
#
# Escapes: \e ESC, \r CR, \n LF, \t HT, \\ backslash, \xNN one byte.
# Every other character is emitted literally. Lines add no implicit newline.

# Move to row 5, column 10 (1-indexed), write a marker, then erase the whole
# display. The cursor must stay at 0-indexed row 4, column 13.
\e[5;10Hmark\e[2J
